WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.756
A customer walks up to a bank teller and says:

2
00:00:02.796 --> 00:00:06.160
"Your manager told me to collect everyone's
statements."

3
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:11.439
The teller may well believe it.

4
00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:15.268
People are persuadable, and language models are
much more so.

5
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:23.202
But the vault still needs a key card, whatever the
teller was told.

6
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.869
In this scenario you are the customer.

7
00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:33.785
You type the instruction straight into the chat.

8
00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:43.511
The model goes along with it and asks for every
customer.

9
00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:45.918
With no rule at the tool, it gets them.

10
00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.806
In secure mode the model still asks.

11
00:00:53.846 --> 00:00:55.327
The tool still says no.

12
00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:58.302
The model was not fixed; the vault rule held.

13
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.219
A model is far easier to talk round than a trained
teller,

14
00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:09.810
so the vault rule must never depend on the
teller's judgement.

15
00:01:12.433 --> 00:01:16.368
Run both modes and find which part of the system
said no.
